src/spextractor.cpp originated as a TOPP tool inside the OpenMS source tree and
was extracted into this standalone repository. It uses OpenMS classes including
MassTraceDetection, ElutionPeakDetection, PeakPickerIM, BrukerTimsFile and
FullSwathFileConsumer, and retains OpenMS's BSD-3-Clause terms.

Algorithmic ideas were reviewed against, but no code was taken from:

  the reference implementation (Nesvizhskii Lab)     -- pseudo-MS/MS extraction from diaPASEF
  AlphaDIA (Mann Lab, Apache-2.0) -- feature-free extraction; the log-sum co-elution
                                     statistic here is an independent reimplementation
                                     of a published idea, not a port
  DIA-NN                          -- used only to produce reference annotations
